    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #290\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to branch `bb/relay-106-inbox-pipeline-07-07-render-inbox-item-thr_88c3ic8mqn`.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplements issue #106: registers the `journal-inbox` view type and caches each Journal day's related Inbox items in `items.computed`, invalidating/recomputing after capture, proposal transitions, and deletion.\n\n- **`views/journalInboxViewType.ts`**: registers the `journal-inbox` view type (config: `inboxDatabaseId`, `journalDayRelationKey`, `computedKey`), following the same registration pattern as the existing `temporal-switcher`/`mailbox-client` view types.\n- **`inbox/journalInboxCompute.ts`**: the computed-cache mechanism — declares `JOURNAL_INBOX_COMPUTED_KEY = \"inboxItems\"`, builds a canonical, display-ready list of Inbox items scoped to one Journal day purely via the `journalDay` relation (excluding soft-deleted items, resolving each item's type and current proposal status as raw canonical values, not localized text), and writes/invalidates it through `writeComputed`/`notifyInvalidation` — mirroring the existing rollup engine's enqueue/recompute pattern with a new deduped `journalInboxRecompute` graphile-worker task.\n- Wired the new task into `@semprec/queue`'s `CORE_TASK_NAMES` and `worker.ts`; declared the computed key and registered the view type during seeding (`seedInboxPipeline.ts`/`seedSystem.ts`).\n- Hooked recompute triggers into all three required invalidation points: capture (`inboxStore.ts`), update/deletion (`inboxTickAction.ts`'s tick handler — a soft-deleted item's relation edge still resolves), and proposal transitions (`proposalActions.ts`'s confirm/reject/revise).\n- Deliberately did not persist a `journal-inbox` view row during seeding since no Journal frontend exists yet in this repo, and doing so would have collided with existing tests asserting exactly one view per seeded database.\n- Added `__tests__/journalInboxCompute.test.ts` (8 tests) covering view-type registration, computed-key collision guarding, day-scoping, type/status resolution, and cache updates after capture, confirm, reject, and deletion.\n\nVerified: full workspace build (`pnpm -r run build`) clean; full test suite (`npx vitest run`) 321/321 tests passed.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
